Program Bug_2_45_InitKrill_InterruptsNotRestored;
// Bug 2.45: Methods6502::InitKrill (methods6502.cpp ~2302) calls
// DisableInterrupts(as) (masking the CIA timer IRQs) and then emits a
// literal `sei` immediately after copying Krill's loader into place, but
// never emits a matching `cli` anywhere in the routine - the same
// "disable, no matching re-enable" shape already catalogued for
// CopyCharsetFromRom (bug 2.39). A program that calls InitKrill() and
// then needs interrupts running (e.g. a raster IRQ) is left with
// interrupts masked until it re-enables them itself.
//
// Verified via a static check on the generated .asm, not the runtime
// php/pla register-peek 2.39 uses (see the companion .asmcheck file):
// InitKrill's own installer (`jsr $3000`, the incbin'd
// krill_installer.bin) genuinely talks to the 1541 drive over the real
// IEC protocol to install Krill's drive-side loader counterpart - running
// it through headless VICE with no disk image mounted hangs forever
// waiting for a response that never comes (confirmed live: no
// results.bin ever appears, even with a generous timeout), unlike every
// other builtin in this suite, none of which depend on real device I/O.
// A plain text check sidesteps this: confirmed live that the generated
// .asm contains InitKrill's own `sei` (right after the "; Init Krill"
// comment) with no `cli` anywhere in the whole program - this snippet
// calls no other builtin that would legitimately emit one either, so the
// mnemonic's total absence is exactly the documented bug, not a
// coincidence of an otherwise-cli-free program.
@use KrillsLoader $0200 $2000 $3000

begin
	InitKrill();
	loop();
end.
